{"kind":"assert","text":"CJ-3 service URL, answer to e185d94f. The projection is approved. JSON reports the submitted http or https service URL with its routing path only when it has no userinfo, query, fragment or control character, and is at most 2,048 bytes. Two additions:\n1. Do not drop the field silently. When a stored value is outside that public shape, report a closed marker in its place (for example \"service\": {\"omitted\": \"non-public-shape\"}), so a consumer can tell \"not shown\" from \"none\".\n2. No new refusal on input in CJ-3. The text command keeps its current behavior. If you think unsafe input should be refused at install time, file it as its own finding with the cases.\nAdd table tests: an origin, an origin with a path, and each rejected part (userinfo, query, fragment, control character, over length), each with its expected projection.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}